WEBVTT

00:05:58.913 --> 00:06:01.329
who'd moved, sometimes
from multiple places,

00:06:01.371 --> 00:06:03.288
to live in the same household.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:05.413
Migration seemed
to be common among the Maya

00:06:05.454 --> 00:06:07.954
and many ancient civilizations.

00:06:07.996 --> 00:06:10.704
But we can move forward in time
to the year 1493,

00:06:10.746 --> 00:06:13.329
when Christopher Columbus
set off on his second voyage

00:06:13.371 --> 00:06:15.163
to establish a trading outpost.

00:06:15.204 --> 00:06:21.329
He left with 17 ships and 1,200 men,
nobility, clergy, sailors and craftsmen

00:06:21.371 --> 00:06:23.913
to establish what
we now know as La Isabela,

00:06:23.954 --> 00:06:25.496
named after Queen Isabella,

00:06:25.538 --> 00:06:27.788
in the northern part
of the Dominican Republic,

00:06:27.829 --> 00:06:30.621
or La Española, as they called it then.